1
00:01:33,470 --> 00:01:35,960
You should leave Weechana.

2
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:40,319
Otherwise, you will be exhausted,
and your effort will go to waste.

3
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:42,259
Because I don't like you.

4
00:01:42,259 --> 00:01:45,215
The others may be a better match for him
more than me.

5
00:01:45,215 --> 00:01:50,500
But I will prove to you you
why your grandson picked me.

6
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:10,597
- Grandma!
- Mom!

7
00:02:10,597 --> 00:02:12,398
Mom!

8
00:02:13,296 --> 00:02:15,840
- Grandma?
- Mom!

9
00:02:15,840 --> 00:02:18,011
Excuse me, please step back.

10
00:02:18,011 --> 00:02:19,190
Give us some room.

11
00:02:19,190 --> 00:02:21,184
- Are you okay?
- Oh my God! Call the ambulance.

12
00:02:21,184 --> 00:02:23,688
What happened? Get a doctor.

13
00:02:23,688 --> 00:02:28,355
I don't feel faint.
My knees just wobbled, that's all.

14
00:02:28,355 --> 00:02:31,220
For a moment, I couldn't feel my legs.

15
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:33,120
Just get me to the couch.

16
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:34,387
Yes, Grandma.

17
00:02:35,430 --> 00:02:36,600
Easy, Mom.

18
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:39,360
Thank you.

19
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:44,615
Slowly, Grandma.

20
00:02:47,471 --> 00:02:50,440
Okay, thank you.

21
00:02:54,504 --> 00:03:01,299
I thought I'd ask Eva
to take me to the couch.

22
00:03:01,299 --> 00:03:04,722
But she said that I was strong enough

23
00:03:04,722 --> 00:03:07,590
to walk to the couch myself.

24
00:03:07,590 --> 00:03:11,600
And I didn't know where she went.

25
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:17,694
I tried to get to the couch myself, but...

26
00:03:17,694 --> 00:03:20,640
my knees just got weak.

27
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,574
- Nicole, darling.
- Yeah?

28
00:03:30,574 --> 00:03:33,589
- Can you take me to the other room?
- Sure.

29
00:03:35,248 --> 00:03:37,456
I'm sorry, everyone.

30
00:03:37,456 --> 00:03:39,195
I hope I didn't ruin your evening.

31
00:03:39,195 --> 00:03:40,544
I'm sorry.

32
00:03:40,544 --> 00:03:42,680
Let's go, darling.

33
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,214
Slowly.

34
00:03:57,249 --> 00:03:58,900
Dad?

35
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:01,858
Grandma didn't tell me
that she needed to rest.

36
00:04:05,586 --> 00:04:08,034
Are you accusing her of lying?

37
00:04:10,387 --> 00:04:13,502
When you're around the elderly,

38
00:04:13,502 --> 00:04:16,184
you should try to read their minds.

39
00:04:16,184 --> 00:04:20,424
Her lips say one thing,
but her mind says another.

40
00:04:20,424 --> 00:04:24,840
Grandma is the heart and soul of this house.

41
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:28,500
We need to take good care of her.

42
00:04:54,136 --> 00:04:56,126
It seems like you're not used to this.

43
00:04:56,126 --> 00:04:57,315
What?

44
00:04:57,315 --> 00:04:59,600
I'm cool. I'm good with it.

45
00:05:04,622 --> 00:05:06,624
Where were you about to go?

46
00:05:09,595 --> 00:05:11,830
Eva asked me to go outside with her.

47
00:05:11,830 --> 00:05:15,880
Nonsense, you should teach her some manners.

48
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:18,035
I won't pursue the matter of her
not attending to me during the party.

49
00:05:18,035 --> 00:05:20,894
But I'm dismayed
that she wants you to accompany her outside

50
00:05:20,894 --> 00:05:23,840
when we are still entertaining our guests.

51
00:05:24,467 --> 00:05:26,478
I understand.

52
00:05:26,478 --> 00:05:27,979
You need to talk to her.

53
00:05:27,979 --> 00:05:32,365
I don't like people
who can't behave properly.

54
00:05:40,715 --> 00:05:42,313
You feel better?

55
00:06:05,070 --> 00:06:08,560
Can you stop the car? I need to talk to you.

56
00:06:11,502 --> 00:06:13,891
Let's talk at your place.

57
00:06:13,891 --> 00:06:17,200
I don't think so.
Domino will stay over tonight.

58
00:06:26,695 --> 00:06:29,086
Before I went over to you,

59
00:06:29,086 --> 00:06:31,625
your grandma said that she didn't like me.

60
00:06:34,797 --> 00:06:37,400
Everyone knows about this.

61
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,937
I know that.

62
00:06:39,846 --> 00:06:41,798
But this time,

63
00:06:41,798 --> 00:06:45,000
she also said
that she prefers Nicole over me.

64
00:06:49,376 --> 00:06:51,641
- Come on.
- Wee.

65
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:56,138
We've dated for two years now.

66
00:06:57,640 --> 00:06:59,852
And I've tried everything.

67
00:07:00,656 --> 00:07:03,008
I changed the way I dress, the way I talk,

68
00:07:03,008 --> 00:07:05,296
how I conduct myself in interviews,
my dining etiquette.

69
00:07:05,296 --> 00:07:09,411
I changed everything,
including how I sit, stand and lie down.

70
00:07:09,411 --> 00:07:12,487
I tried to remember who your guests are
at the parties.

71
00:07:12,487 --> 00:07:14,590
There must be 20-30 people to remember,
and I did.

72
00:07:14,590 --> 00:07:16,974
You told me to say hi to them, and I did.

73
00:07:16,974 --> 00:07:19,171
I helped out with your work. Everything.

74
00:07:19,171 --> 00:07:21,134
Look at me now. It's been two years,

75
00:07:21,134 --> 00:07:23,454
and your grandma still calls me
a food vendor's niece.

76
00:07:23,454 --> 00:07:27,086
Eva, we talked about this.

77
00:07:27,086 --> 00:07:29,595
We will fight together.

78
00:07:29,595 --> 00:07:33,900
I saw your effort
and I appreciate you for that.

79
00:07:36,422 --> 00:07:38,720
But if you're trying to win Grandma's heart,

80
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:41,440
your EQ needs to be better than this.

81
00:07:43,712 --> 00:07:45,347
Eva.

82
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:49,614
Eva!

83
00:07:49,614 --> 00:07:52,658
Don't do this, please calm down.

84
00:07:52,658 --> 00:07:54,366
How much EQ is required for the situation?

85
00:07:54,366 --> 00:07:56,080
Your grandma said to my face

86
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:57,986
that I should break up with you
because Nicole suits you better.

87
00:07:57,986 --> 00:08:03,080
- How much EQ is required, huh?
- You need to know that Grandma is old.

88
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:04,870
And you shouldn't have
let her fall like that.

89
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:08,118
Your grandma is strong enough
to walk on a golf course.

90
00:08:08,118 --> 00:08:11,072
How did her knees suddenly get weak?

91
00:08:11,072 --> 00:08:13,800
- Where did she learn her acting skills from?
- Eva!

92
00:08:27,536 --> 00:08:29,408
We should go.

93
00:08:31,144 --> 00:08:32,750
I have work tomorrow.

94
00:09:02,971 --> 00:09:06,720
Why are you home early?

95
00:09:08,054 --> 00:09:09,873
What?

96
00:09:09,873 --> 00:09:12,049
What happened this time?

97
00:09:13,406 --> 00:09:17,235
She pretended to fall
and blamed it all on me.

98
00:09:17,235 --> 00:09:20,691
Oh my goodness!

99
00:09:20,691 --> 00:09:22,008
This is the perfect plot for a soap opera.

100
00:09:22,008 --> 00:09:24,111
Such an ancient trick.

101
00:09:26,311 --> 00:09:28,281
Are you okay?

102
00:09:29,310 --> 00:09:30,750
Sure.

103
00:09:35,482 --> 00:09:37,338
I love him.

104
00:09:38,502 --> 00:09:40,303
I know that...

105
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:43,360
he isn't perfect.

106
00:09:45,152 --> 00:09:48,480
But he's nice to me
and I want to keep fighting.

107
00:09:52,302 --> 00:09:54,450
I need to star in this film.

108
00:09:55,832 --> 00:09:58,942
If everything turns out well like I expected,

109
00:09:58,942 --> 00:10:01,670
I will have a chance to join a film festival.

110
00:10:01,670 --> 00:10:03,563
Luxury brands will book me,

111
00:10:03,563 --> 00:10:06,456
and it will be a whole next step for me.

112
00:10:06,456 --> 00:10:10,800
His family will then probably
be more willing to accept me.

113
00:10:14,974 --> 00:10:20,766
Look, his grandma didn't focus
on the present.

114
00:10:20,766 --> 00:10:24,576
She focused way back to your family origins.

115
00:10:25,294 --> 00:10:27,855
No matter how good you try to be,

116
00:10:27,855 --> 00:10:33,840
nothing will work
if she keeps focusing on your upbringing.

117
00:10:35,344 --> 00:10:38,600
I can't choose my mother.

118
00:10:40,163 --> 00:10:43,960
I can only show them
how great I am right now.

119
00:10:51,664 --> 00:10:54,560
Let's go. Go, go.

120
00:10:55,643 --> 00:10:57,270
You need to shower.

121
00:10:57,270 --> 00:10:59,408
You'll be meeting a director tomorrow.

122
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:02,056
You need to look pretty.

123
00:11:02,056 --> 00:11:05,747
Don't care about the rest.
Just focus on being pretty, okay?

124
00:11:05,747 --> 00:11:07,304
Go! Go! Go!

125
00:11:07,304 --> 00:11:09,200
Go take a shower.

126
00:11:10,355 --> 00:11:12,427
Look at you, you're so beautiful,

127
00:11:12,427 --> 00:11:14,400
as if you were an angel in your past life.

128
00:11:15,282 --> 00:11:17,260
Oh my goodness! Can you do a twirl for me?

129
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:19,542
One more time, make a full turn.

130
00:11:19,542 --> 00:11:23,320
Oh my goodness! Whoa!

131
00:11:24,128 --> 00:11:26,320
Good night.

132
00:11:36,852 --> 00:11:39,908
So there might be some changes
to the script along the way,

133
00:11:39,908 --> 00:11:41,566
but there's nothing to worry about.

134
00:11:41,566 --> 00:11:43,900
It's just part of the process.

135
00:11:47,820 --> 00:11:49,718
Thank you.

136
00:11:49,718 --> 00:11:51,344
I'm try my best.

137
00:11:52,192 --> 00:11:55,019
Mai, can you ask him

138
00:11:55,019 --> 00:12:00,694
about the character's personalities
that I should learn?

139
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:02,480
She'd like to know

140
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:06,086
if there are any specific details
you'd like for the character.

141
00:12:06,086 --> 00:12:08,758
So she can start preparing right away.

142
00:12:08,758 --> 00:12:12,650
Well, her character is a bit of a hot-head,

143
00:12:12,650 --> 00:12:16,822
talks fast,
and doesn't like being misunderstood.

144
00:12:16,822 --> 00:12:20,880
I want the language to feel fast and natural.

145
00:12:22,998 --> 00:12:25,382
- Yeah?
- It's the language.

146
00:12:25,382 --> 00:12:28,111
The character is a hot-head,
so she will need to talk fast.

147
00:12:28,111 --> 00:12:30,448
- And she likes to argue.
- Got it.

148
00:12:30,448 --> 00:12:35,720
Hot-headed, talks fast, likes to argue.

149
00:12:36,466 --> 00:12:38,094
Got it.

150
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:41,854
Actually,

151
00:12:41,854 --> 00:12:44,894
May told me
that there are some adjustments in the script.

152
00:12:44,894 --> 00:12:49,025
The lead actress was born in Thailand

153
00:12:49,025 --> 00:12:51,087
but she has spent time abroad for years.

154
00:12:51,087 --> 00:12:54,435
Therefore, the accent is really important.

155
00:12:54,435 --> 00:12:56,451
It's more than just speaking level.

156
00:12:56,451 --> 00:12:59,662
He wants Eva to read the script for him

157
00:12:59,662 --> 00:13:01,491
and he will make a decision later.

158
00:13:01,491 --> 00:13:02,856
What?

159
00:13:04,926 --> 00:13:06,947
Make a decision later? Does it mean

160
00:13:06,947 --> 00:13:12,531
that I might not get the role
if my accent isn't good enough?

161
00:13:13,507 --> 00:13:15,779
She wants to know if she won't get the role

162
00:13:15,779 --> 00:13:18,168
if her English isn't good enough.

163
00:13:18,168 --> 00:13:21,412
Well, it needs to be there.

164
00:13:21,412 --> 00:13:24,522
But the director is willing
to give you more time to prepare.

165
00:13:24,522 --> 00:13:27,675
And in the mean time, I want to be honest,

166
00:13:27,675 --> 00:13:30,965
I might need to keep other options open
as a backup.

167
00:13:34,198 --> 00:13:36,043
Language is really important.

168
00:13:36,043 --> 00:13:39,955
The director will give you time
for you to practice.

169
00:13:39,955 --> 00:13:43,992
But they still need to cast others
as a backup.

170
00:13:46,788 --> 00:13:48,413
I got it.

171
00:13:50,099 --> 00:13:54,064
Thank you for give me time.
I will try my best.

172
00:13:54,976 --> 00:13:58,720
She's a good actress. She's the best one.

173
00:14:01,019 --> 00:14:04,608
If I can't make them satisfied,
I will lose this role.

174
00:14:04,608 --> 00:14:05,723
I know,

175
00:14:05,723 --> 00:14:11,158
she is ready to get another person
to take over your role.

176
00:14:11,158 --> 00:14:12,283
Where's Pun?

177
00:14:12,283 --> 00:14:13,947
I'll ask him to teach me tomorrow.

178
00:14:13,947 --> 00:14:16,000
I need to get the role.

179
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,320
Sure, okay.

180
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:34,680
[Eva Yanin]

181
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:36,800
[Eva Yanin]

182
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:39,000
[From street vendor's niece
to Number 1 superstar]

183
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,520
[Ava's fortune skyrockets]

184
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:42,345
[She enjoys a bright romance
with a young politician]

185
00:14:42,345 --> 00:14:44,200
[The life of Eva Yanin:
From provincial kid to leading superstar]

186
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:50,160
[From the niece of a food vendor,
to Number 1 superstar]

187
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:55,759
[She's lucky in career and in love]

188
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:57,280
[Eva is dating a politician]

189
00:15:03,832 --> 00:15:05,799
You're worried
that Eva would find out about this?

190
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:08,694
When will she know
that you're also dating me?

191
00:15:08,694 --> 00:15:09,479
What for?

192
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:12,800
So she will know
that she's got herself a competitor.

193
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:23,719
[Ruam Thai Chana]

194
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:26,560
[Vote for Number 2]
[Uniting hearts, moving forward to victory]

195
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:28,422
I think a picture of me
with my arms crossing like this one

196
00:15:28,422 --> 00:15:32,120
makes me unreachable and a little bit boring.

197
00:15:33,750 --> 00:15:37,150
But I like this one,
with my hand in my pocket.

198
00:15:38,278 --> 00:15:40,472
I look more relaxed in there.

199
00:15:40,472 --> 00:15:42,320
Dad, what do you think?

200
00:15:48,715 --> 00:15:52,788
Can you put my face in one of them?

201
00:15:52,788 --> 00:15:56,105
Our old supporters will know
that I'm still around.

202
00:15:59,062 --> 00:16:00,694
Great idea.

203
00:16:00,694 --> 00:16:02,680
I want it done fast.

204
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:11,000
If we're done here,
can I have a moment with my sons?

205
00:16:27,519 --> 00:16:29,937
What is your campaign plan?

206
00:16:32,760 --> 00:16:35,288
I'm thinking of doing some activities
with the young voters.

207
00:16:35,288 --> 00:16:40,406
They need to know that we're on their side.

208
00:16:40,406 --> 00:16:45,388
Young people are more interested in politics
than before.

209
00:16:45,388 --> 00:16:49,480
I want the young voters to be my stronghold.

210
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:53,358
I will organize the band contest.

211
00:16:53,358 --> 00:16:57,272
We will find actors to shoot a short film.

212
00:16:57,272 --> 00:16:59,880
I think it's a good idea.

213
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:05,834
Eva and Pie
should be in charge of entertainment.

214
00:17:05,834 --> 00:17:09,507
I think Pie is more suitable for the job.

215
00:17:09,507 --> 00:17:12,920
Pie is younger and she can
understand people in this age group.

216
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:15,293
Eva's target should be people...

217
00:17:15,293 --> 00:17:17,601
who are 30 years old and older.

218
00:17:17,601 --> 00:17:21,846
People in their thirties are the ones
who form the foundation of support.

219
00:17:23,416 --> 00:17:28,040
They both can help with the campaign.

220
00:17:28,806 --> 00:17:30,155
Okay.

221
00:17:41,528 --> 00:17:43,329
Can you help me?

222
00:17:44,080 --> 00:17:46,844
Can you help me?

223
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,813
Wait a minute.

224
00:17:52,142 --> 00:17:53,930
Wait a minute.

225
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:00,920
[Wee]

226
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:06,440
We are going home.

227
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:08,940
We are going home.

228
00:18:15,505 --> 00:18:17,886
<i>You're still mad at me?</i>

229
00:18:25,243 --> 00:18:28,920
<i>I'm not mad. I know that I was wrong.</i>

230
00:18:30,513 --> 00:18:32,753
But I wasn't wrong.

231
00:18:36,080 --> 00:18:38,662
<i>I have to work out
and study my lines tomorrow.</i>

232
00:18:38,662 --> 00:18:42,000
<i>I need to get some sleep. Talk to you later.</i>

233
00:18:50,272 --> 00:18:53,595
<i>Okay, you should get some rest.</i>

234
00:18:53,595 --> 00:18:55,396
<i>I love you.</i>

235
00:19:02,090 --> 00:19:03,480
Let's get home.

236
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:23,720
[Trending Shows]

237
00:19:47,238 --> 00:19:50,046
Just give her some light training today,
to see how fit she is.

238
00:19:50,046 --> 00:19:51,443
Do a check on her body assessment.

239
00:19:51,443 --> 00:19:53,048
No need to be too hard on her, okay?

240
00:19:53,048 --> 00:19:54,664
Sure, don't worry.

241
00:19:54,664 --> 00:19:57,280
Don't forget to tell her
that I'll get better soon

242
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:58,475
so I can train her.

243
00:19:58,475 --> 00:20:00,630
- Okay?
- Sure.

244
00:20:00,630 --> 00:20:02,166
We'll talk about that later.

245
00:20:02,166 --> 00:20:03,680
Here.

246
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:04,976
Wow, looks good.

247
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:08,086
You need to eat enough protein.

248
00:20:08,086 --> 00:20:10,128
And you can't drink any coffee.

249
00:20:10,128 --> 00:20:12,103
It decreases intestinal calcium absorption.

250
00:20:12,103 --> 00:20:14,367
- Got it?
- Yes, Chef.

251
00:20:18,995 --> 00:20:20,840
Whoa! Super healthy.

252
00:22:12,475 --> 00:22:15,720
We have a new project to discuss later, okay?

253
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:16,960
Got it.

254
00:22:16,960 --> 00:22:19,332
Jeez, the door's so heavy.

255
00:22:25,646 --> 00:22:27,102
Hey.

256
00:22:27,102 --> 00:22:28,254
Did you hear that?

257
00:22:28,254 --> 00:22:30,640
Yeah, I did.

258
00:22:40,038 --> 00:22:41,552
Should we go?

259
00:22:41,552 --> 00:22:43,163
Let's go.

260
00:22:43,163 --> 00:22:44,601
Follow me.

261
00:22:46,459 --> 00:22:47,526
Hey.

262
00:22:47,526 --> 00:22:48,920
What? Don't call me.

263
00:22:48,920 --> 00:22:51,800
You need to keep it down or they'll know!

264
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:12,412
Hey!

265
00:23:31,915 --> 00:23:35,662
Hey! How did you get in here?

266
00:23:35,662 --> 00:23:37,907
Hey!

267
00:23:37,907 --> 00:23:40,520
I gave him the key, I totally forgot.

268
00:23:40,520 --> 00:23:42,321
I'm sorry.

269
00:23:43,143 --> 00:23:46,235
But you can't take a shower here.

270
00:23:46,235 --> 00:23:47,952
This is Eva's bathroom.

271
00:23:47,952 --> 00:23:51,392
That's right, and you can't
walk around naked like this.

272
00:23:51,392 --> 00:23:54,400
- It's inappropriate.
- I'm sorry.

273
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:56,223
I'm sorry.

274
00:23:56,223 --> 00:23:59,167
Okay, I'm done.

275
00:24:00,971 --> 00:24:03,039
I jogged all the way from Boat's place,

276
00:24:03,039 --> 00:24:04,654
and I had sweat a lot.

277
00:24:04,654 --> 00:24:07,944
I didn't know you'd be here early.
I'm really sorry.

278
00:24:07,944 --> 00:24:11,347
- I forgot that...
- You can run on your way back.

279
00:24:11,347 --> 00:24:14,228
So you don't need to use my bathroom.

280
00:24:14,228 --> 00:24:16,394
Okay, got it.

281
00:24:18,015 --> 00:24:20,174
Eva, you should get ready.

282
00:24:20,174 --> 00:24:22,120
I need to talk to him.

283
00:24:25,112 --> 00:24:27,359
About work.

284
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:32,894
A tutor?

285
00:24:32,894 --> 00:24:35,294
That's right.

286
00:24:35,294 --> 00:24:39,278
I'd like you to be her tutor,
for her English script.

287
00:24:39,278 --> 00:24:40,499
Here's the plot.

288
00:24:40,499 --> 00:24:42,560
A woman was born in Thailand,

289
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:44,272
but she has spent her life
in a foreign country for years.

290
00:24:44,272 --> 00:24:47,300
Then she comes back to Thailand
to get revenge for her younger sister.

291
00:24:47,300 --> 00:24:48,401
Seriously?

292
00:24:48,401 --> 00:24:50,307
Yeah, really.

293
00:24:50,307 --> 00:24:53,600
This is the accent that Eva needs to learn.

294
00:24:54,267 --> 00:24:55,494
Please listen to me,

295
00:24:55,494 --> 00:24:58,310
you and your friend are very well-rounded.

296
00:24:58,310 --> 00:25:02,196
You two can be personal trainer,
chef and tutor.

297
00:25:02,196 --> 00:25:05,134
We don't have much time,

298
00:25:05,134 --> 00:25:08,043
and I'd like you to focus
on her English speaking skill.

299
00:25:08,043 --> 00:25:10,539
Boat is in a cast right now.

300
00:25:10,539 --> 00:25:12,840
So you need to train her and be her tutor.

301
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:14,441
When Boat comes back,

302
00:25:14,441 --> 00:25:16,866
you can focus only on being her tutor.

303
00:25:17,686 --> 00:25:19,288
But I can't...

304
00:25:19,288 --> 00:25:21,774
No buts, please.

305
00:25:21,774 --> 00:25:23,680
Please give your code.

306
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:27,307
Code?

307
00:25:27,307 --> 00:25:28,682
Yeah, your rate.

308
00:25:28,682 --> 00:25:30,550
My rate?

309
00:25:30,550 --> 00:25:31,958
Code.

310
00:25:31,958 --> 00:25:33,759
Quote!

311
00:25:34,560 --> 00:25:36,856
- Quote.
- Yeah... yeah, quote.

312
00:25:37,931 --> 00:25:40,600
<i>Go ahead, man. What are you waiting for?</i>

313
00:25:40,600 --> 00:25:44,520
- <i>But...</i>
- You will earn more money.

314
00:25:44,520 --> 00:25:47,582
After this, you can start your own business.

315
00:25:47,582 --> 00:25:48,819
What about this?

316
00:25:48,819 --> 00:25:50,728
I'll calculate the rate for you,

317
00:25:50,728 --> 00:25:53,464
and see how much you should charge them.

318
00:25:53,464 --> 00:25:55,215
In the meantime, you need to tell them,

319
00:25:55,215 --> 00:25:57,006
"I need more time to think."

320
00:25:57,006 --> 00:25:59,864
Stalling for time, you know?

321
00:25:59,864 --> 00:26:03,480
Tell them you need more time, okay?

322
00:26:03,480 --> 00:26:05,281
Okay, okay.

323
00:26:08,168 --> 00:26:11,974
Let me see, how much should we charge?

324
00:26:15,334 --> 00:26:17,433
What do you think?

325
00:26:17,433 --> 00:26:20,675
About me being a tutor,

326
00:26:20,675 --> 00:26:23,315
are you sure that I'm qualified to teach her?

327
00:26:23,315 --> 00:26:24,280
Of course...

328
00:26:24,280 --> 00:26:27,560
If she has totally no background in English,

329
00:26:28,200 --> 00:26:31,480
shouldn't you find
a professional tutor for her?

330
00:26:31,480 --> 00:26:34,328
I don't want anyone to know
that Eva needs a tutor.

331
00:26:34,328 --> 00:26:35,651
What?

332
00:26:36,462 --> 00:26:38,920
I know that you don't get it,
and I don't expect you to.

333
00:26:38,920 --> 00:26:43,544
It's complicated in the world of celebrities.

334
00:26:43,544 --> 00:26:45,502
I see.

335
00:26:45,502 --> 00:26:48,120
Just trust me,

336
00:26:48,120 --> 00:26:50,840
you're the most qualified
under these circumstances.

337
00:26:50,840 --> 00:26:52,520
This is the script.

338
00:26:52,520 --> 00:26:54,521
Here, take it.

339
00:26:54,521 --> 00:26:55,519
Just have a look.

340
00:26:55,520 --> 00:26:57,199
[The Black Rose]

341
00:26:57,200 --> 00:26:59,918
Oh my! It's time, I need to run some errands.

342
00:26:59,918 --> 00:27:01,982
I'll be back late afternoon.

343
00:27:01,982 --> 00:27:05,680
Please take care of her, the script is fun.

344
00:27:08,760 --> 00:27:10,040
[The Black Rose]

345
00:27:13,744 --> 00:27:16,550
Eva, can I talk to you?

346
00:27:16,550 --> 00:27:17,720
About?

347
00:27:17,720 --> 00:27:19,252
Your conversational skills.

348
00:27:21,627 --> 00:27:23,164
What about it?

349
00:27:24,144 --> 00:27:26,840
I don't know about your level.

350
00:27:26,840 --> 00:27:28,800
I don't know how to teach you.

351
00:27:34,772 --> 00:27:36,573
You can just...

352
00:27:37,374 --> 00:27:39,552
let me repeat the lines after you.

353
00:27:39,552 --> 00:27:41,640
And I can imitate your accent.

354
00:27:42,937 --> 00:27:45,489
Like teaching a parrot to speak?

355
00:27:48,280 --> 00:27:50,106
That's rude.

356
00:27:50,907 --> 00:27:53,482
No, I just want to know
what method you prefer.

357
00:27:53,482 --> 00:27:55,974
Hey, I'm not a professional tutor.

358
00:27:55,974 --> 00:27:59,840
And I need to tutor you
when I know nothing about it.

359
00:27:59,840 --> 00:28:01,923
Eva, I can't do it.

360
00:28:01,923 --> 00:28:04,008
Many people will want this chance
to work with me.

361
00:28:04,008 --> 00:28:07,171
You can hire a new tutor then.

362
00:28:07,171 --> 00:28:09,654
I can go back to my original position.

363
00:28:09,654 --> 00:28:11,168
Okay?

364
00:28:13,758 --> 00:28:17,960
Right, we will start
with your physical fitness test.

365
00:28:19,016 --> 00:28:20,817
We'll start with...

366
00:28:21,774 --> 00:28:23,200
jumping rope.

367
00:28:28,142 --> 00:28:31,920
Why do you want to know so much
about my conversational skills?

368
00:28:33,339 --> 00:28:36,042
I'm only hiring you
to help me speak English fluently.

369
00:28:42,526 --> 00:28:45,560
You don't have to know everything.

370
00:28:46,337 --> 00:28:48,138
It's totally fine.

371
00:28:49,027 --> 00:28:53,120
There are hundreds of things
that you're better than me.

372
00:28:55,059 --> 00:28:56,449
More than that.

373
00:28:57,503 --> 00:28:59,231
Okay.

374
00:28:59,231 --> 00:29:00,899
More than that.

375
00:29:06,104 --> 00:29:07,905
We're in the same boat.

376
00:29:09,277 --> 00:29:11,016
If you'd like me to tutor you,

377
00:29:11,016 --> 00:29:13,817
you need to tell me what you know,
and what you don't know.

378
00:29:15,401 --> 00:29:17,657
I don't focus on money only.

379
00:29:18,744 --> 00:29:20,545
I want you to be good at it.

380
00:29:36,206 --> 00:29:37,928
Are you ready?

381
00:29:37,928 --> 00:29:39,436
I don't know how.

382
00:29:40,558 --> 00:29:42,209
Teach me.

383
00:29:43,800 --> 00:29:46,520
[Ruam Thai Chana]

384
00:29:53,016 --> 00:29:54,817
Excuse me, sir.

385
00:29:58,328 --> 00:30:00,159
Our people reported

386
00:30:00,160 --> 00:30:05,604
that there are many photos of you and Ginny
in the stalker's computer.

387
00:30:07,816 --> 00:30:10,000
They've sent me some of them.

388
00:30:27,704 --> 00:30:30,344
Who saw these pictures besides you?

389
00:30:30,971 --> 00:30:34,105
Only the investigation team,
but they're working for us.

390
00:30:34,105 --> 00:30:35,906
We can handle them.

391
00:30:37,560 --> 00:30:40,048
Tell them to delete everything.

392
00:30:40,048 --> 00:30:42,760
These photos can't be leaked.

393
00:30:43,974 --> 00:30:45,920
My dad can't find out about them.

394
00:30:47,112 --> 00:30:50,920
Eva can't know about them either.

395
00:30:51,591 --> 00:30:53,392
Yes, sir.

396
00:31:02,886 --> 00:31:07,520
Actually, I don't want to learn it
only for my work.

397
00:31:11,923 --> 00:31:16,168
Many Thai people are starting
to speak English,

398
00:31:16,168 --> 00:31:19,889
and those who can't,
will lose opportunities for something.

399
00:31:19,889 --> 00:31:24,280
People who speak English
with a strong Thai accent

400
00:31:24,280 --> 00:31:26,515
will be looked down on.

401
00:31:26,515 --> 00:31:28,084
Why's that?

402
00:31:35,803 --> 00:31:40,278
Actually, the westerners don't care
about dialects.

403
00:31:40,278 --> 00:31:43,658
Speaking English
with Japanese, Chinese or Singaporean accents

404
00:31:43,658 --> 00:31:45,291
are quite charming.

405
00:31:45,291 --> 00:31:47,035
It's like when they visit our country,

406
00:31:47,035 --> 00:31:51,680
they speak broken Thai
and we find them adorable.

407
00:31:53,032 --> 00:31:56,450
Thai people don't find
other Thai people adorable.

408
00:31:56,450 --> 00:31:59,790
It becomes an indicator of your class,

409
00:31:59,790 --> 00:32:02,880
and you will be put
in a specific social status.

410
00:32:04,115 --> 00:32:05,916
Nonsense.

411
00:32:09,438 --> 00:32:12,120
Welcome to this world.

412
00:32:24,590 --> 00:32:27,171
Before jumping rope,
you should warm up for 10 minutes,

413
00:32:27,171 --> 00:32:30,480
to warm up the body and prevent injury.

414
00:32:32,891 --> 00:32:34,534
Did you understand it?

415
00:32:34,534 --> 00:32:35,817
Nope.

416
00:32:36,566 --> 00:32:38,022
Can you speak slower?

417
00:32:38,022 --> 00:32:40,358
You spoke too fast and I was startled.

418
00:32:40,358 --> 00:32:42,539
Okay, okay.

419
00:32:42,539 --> 00:32:45,800
Before jumping rope,
you should warm up for 10 minutes

420
00:32:45,800 --> 00:32:48,760
to warm up the body and prevent injury.

421
00:32:52,843 --> 00:32:54,844
Before jumping rope...

422
00:32:54,844 --> 00:32:55,931
Yeah.

423
00:32:55,931 --> 00:32:59,869
I need to warm up for 10 minutes.

424
00:32:59,869 --> 00:33:01,841
Yes.

425
00:33:02,534 --> 00:33:05,360
I didn't get the rest.

426
00:33:06,379 --> 00:33:08,760
To prevent injury.

427
00:33:08,760 --> 00:33:11,320
Prevent, stop it from happening.

428
00:33:11,320 --> 00:33:14,178
Injury, getting hurt.

429
00:33:14,178 --> 00:33:16,579
Injury. Getting hurt.

430
00:33:17,910 --> 00:33:21,566
Okay, you need to widen your vocabulary.

431
00:33:21,566 --> 00:33:25,167
When you're trying to say it in English,
you need to know what it means.

432
00:33:28,446 --> 00:33:34,123
I want to be able to understand, speak,
respond, and have your accent.

433
00:33:34,123 --> 00:33:35,579
Okay, I got you.

434
00:33:35,579 --> 00:33:39,280
You need to understand about grammar.

435
00:33:40,216 --> 00:33:42,102
What? Grammar?

436
00:33:42,102 --> 00:33:43,174
Yeah.

437
00:33:43,174 --> 00:33:45,800
I get confused even for a simple sentence.

438
00:33:52,174 --> 00:33:54,175
Okay.

439
00:33:54,175 --> 00:33:57,278
We need to learn for two purposes.

440
00:33:57,278 --> 00:34:00,000
The first one, to learn your lines.

441
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:03,659
Focusing on understanding
the lines, the context, and the accent.

442
00:34:03,659 --> 00:34:05,800
The second one,

443
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:09,480
learning to use it in conversations
in your daily life.

444
00:34:09,480 --> 00:34:10,558
Let's go.

445
00:34:10,558 --> 00:34:12,696
Let's start with a quick warm up.

446
00:34:12,696 --> 00:34:14,840
Two minutes on the jump rope.

447
00:34:14,840 --> 00:34:16,920
10 squats, slow and controlled.

448
00:34:16,920 --> 00:34:19,970
And then let's finish off
with a 30-second plank.

449
00:34:19,970 --> 00:34:21,925
Did you get it?

450
00:34:21,925 --> 00:34:23,531
Nope.

451
00:34:23,531 --> 00:34:26,769
Okay, wait.

452
00:34:26,769 --> 00:34:30,299
Can you try to tell me
that you didn't understand me,

453
00:34:30,299 --> 00:34:32,237
and you need me to say it again?

454
00:34:38,131 --> 00:34:39,600
Again.

455
00:34:43,040 --> 00:34:45,400
Is it, "tell me again"?

456
00:34:48,565 --> 00:34:51,574
Alright, it's not wrong.

457
00:34:51,574 --> 00:34:54,240
But... hold on.

458
00:34:55,025 --> 00:34:59,200
It's not the right way to say it.

459
00:34:59,963 --> 00:35:03,131
You can say...

460
00:35:03,131 --> 00:35:04,960
"Come again?"

461
00:35:04,960 --> 00:35:06,944
Or, "say that again."

462
00:35:06,944 --> 00:35:09,542
Or you can say it informally and short, like,

463
00:35:09,542 --> 00:35:13,008
"What was that?" or, "One more time."

464
00:35:13,008 --> 00:35:16,039
When you don't understand what they say,
or you don't catch it,

465
00:35:16,039 --> 00:35:18,390
you can ask these questions.

466
00:35:18,390 --> 00:35:20,603
It's completely normal.

467
00:35:20,603 --> 00:35:23,160
Okay, let's try it.

468
00:35:24,659 --> 00:35:26,560
Say that again.

469
00:35:28,174 --> 00:35:31,363
Not bad. One more time.

470
00:35:31,363 --> 00:35:33,280
One more time.

471
00:35:42,418 --> 00:35:45,400
Okay, you did great today.

472
00:35:45,400 --> 00:35:47,350
Tomorrow, we'll go running.

473
00:35:47,350 --> 00:35:48,795
Okay.

474
00:35:48,795 --> 00:35:51,200
A run with a view.

475
00:35:51,200 --> 00:35:56,243
You will tell me what the places
along our route are.

476
00:35:56,243 --> 00:35:59,992
The gardens, streets, buildings or whatever.

477
00:35:59,992 --> 00:36:01,811
You need to tell me in English.

478
00:36:01,811 --> 00:36:03,704
That's crazy.

479
00:36:03,704 --> 00:36:05,905
Are you serious?

480
00:36:05,905 --> 00:36:10,088
Sorry, what was that? I don't understand.

481
00:36:10,088 --> 00:36:13,517
English, please.

482
00:36:13,517 --> 00:36:15,171
Crazy.

483
00:36:17,027 --> 00:36:19,320
Are you crazy?

484
00:36:19,320 --> 00:36:21,040
Yeah, you can say that.

485
00:36:21,040 --> 00:36:24,080
Many people would say, "are you nuts?"

486
00:36:24,080 --> 00:36:26,448
- Nuts?
- Yeah.

487
00:36:26,448 --> 00:36:27,915
Like peanuts?

488
00:36:27,915 --> 00:36:29,628
Yeah, like that.

489
00:36:29,628 --> 00:36:32,246
Or, "are you out of your mind?"

490
00:36:32,246 --> 00:36:35,000
You can also say, "are you kidding me?"

491
00:36:35,891 --> 00:36:37,912
- Nuts?
- Yeah.

492
00:36:40,046 --> 00:36:43,440
When I want to call someone

493
00:36:43,440 --> 00:36:46,080
who is very crazy, what should I say?

494
00:36:47,963 --> 00:36:49,931
People who are crazy?

495
00:36:51,286 --> 00:36:53,662
I don't think there's a word for it.

496
00:36:53,662 --> 00:36:56,103
The closest one is, "you're such an idiot."

497
00:36:56,103 --> 00:36:59,751
But it's "idiot",
so it doesn't entirely mean crazy.

498
00:36:59,751 --> 00:37:04,284
I think Thai words are more varied
than English words.

499
00:37:04,284 --> 00:37:07,280
It won't work if you think in Thai
before you speak in English.

500
00:37:08,176 --> 00:37:09,647
Hey!

501
00:37:10,912 --> 00:37:12,287
Wait.

502
00:37:14,205 --> 00:37:17,578
Are you trying to call me crazy?

503
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:21,320
I'm not sure. Did I say it right?

504
00:37:21,992 --> 00:37:24,514
Not exactly.

505
00:37:25,483 --> 00:37:27,850
Not exactly.

506
00:37:32,464 --> 00:37:35,315
Okay. I'll see you tomorrow, early morning.

507
00:37:35,315 --> 00:37:37,116
I'll pick you up at home.

508
00:38:05,635 --> 00:38:07,025
What?

509
00:38:09,352 --> 00:38:10,818
Where is Domino?

510
00:38:11,645 --> 00:38:13,523
She'll be here in 20 minutes.

511
00:38:14,446 --> 00:38:15,872
Okay.

512
00:38:17,083 --> 00:38:20,640
I'll keep you company until she's here.

513
00:38:21,507 --> 00:38:23,037
In case, you get scared.

514
00:38:23,864 --> 00:38:26,779
Okay, thanks.

515
00:39:16,824 --> 00:39:18,331
Hello, Book?

516
00:39:18,331 --> 00:39:19,407
<i>Hello, Eva.</i>

517
00:39:19,407 --> 00:39:21,925
<i>I'm Book, Ginny's manager.</i>

518
00:39:21,925 --> 00:39:23,643
Yeah?

519
00:39:23,643 --> 00:39:25,205
Is everything okay?

520
00:39:25,205 --> 00:39:27,419
I have something important to talk to you.

521
00:39:27,419 --> 00:39:29,480
<i>You need to know about this.</i>

522
00:39:29,480 --> 00:39:31,560
<i>Can you come and meet me?</i>

523
00:39:32,800 --> 00:39:34,320
What's this about?

524
00:39:34,320 --> 00:39:36,600
<i>It's about Ginny and Weechana.</i>

525
00:39:39,509 --> 00:39:41,206
What do you mean?

526
00:39:41,206 --> 00:39:44,134
<i>I don't want to talk on the phone.
We should meet up.</i>

527
00:39:44,134 --> 00:39:47,019
Are you out of your mind?

528
00:39:47,019 --> 00:39:49,720
Ginny's stalker tried to kill me.

529
00:39:49,720 --> 00:39:53,192
And you expect me to meet you alone
without a clue of what's going on?

530
00:39:53,192 --> 00:39:56,880
I'll send you something,
and you'll know what it's about.

531
00:40:02,952 --> 00:40:06,899
<i>Wee, where should we meet up in New York?</i>

532
00:40:06,899 --> 00:40:09,475
<i>This restaurant is really nice.
I'll drop you its location.</i>

533
00:40:09,475 --> 00:40:11,589
<i>Are we just here to eat?</i>

534
00:40:11,589 --> 00:40:13,647
<i>Or are we going to do something else later?</i>

535
00:40:13,647 --> 00:40:15,035
<i>Haha.</i>

536
00:40:15,035 --> 00:40:17,664
<i>I'll take you to have some desserts later.</i>

537
00:40:17,664 --> 00:40:19,880
<i>Ginny took her English courses in New York.</i>

538
00:40:19,880 --> 00:40:24,480
And it was the same time
that Wee was in the US.

539
00:40:31,800 --> 00:40:34,679
<i>If you think that we should meet in person,
call me.</i>

540
00:40:40,963 --> 00:40:45,160
Hey Book, I'll call you later.
I need to talk to you.

541
00:41:15,154 --> 00:41:16,499
You son of a bitch!

542
00:41:17,289 --> 00:41:19,803
Why did you lie to me?

